  "body": "## What is needed\n\nShop-floor users who run quick-op contours, bosses, frames, and pocket finish passes expect to adjust part size slightly at the machine control using the tool wear offset register (`G41`/`G42`).\n\n## Design\n\n- Default quick-op finishing contours, bosses, and frames to `Compensation::Wear` (`crates/motion/src/approach.rs`) when the active post supports cutter compensation.\n- In `Compensation::Wear`, CamCraft writes the cutter-centre path under `G41`/`G42` so the part cuts to nominal size when the control wear register is zero.\n- Keep `Compensation::Computer` automatically when:\n  - The active post does not support `G41`/`G42`.\n  - The operation cuts an open chain (`crates/app/src/operation/contour_sketch.rs`).\n- Seed valid linear lead-in and lead-out lengths (at least one cutter radius, per RS-274 / ISO 6983 startup and cancel rules) so the existing lead refusal law is satisfied by default, and keep the refusal active if the user shortens the lead.\n- Allow the user to switch the operation to `Computer` or `Control` in the normal parameter panel or via MCP.\n\nClean-room rule: based on RS-274 / ISO 6983 cutter radius compensation rules and existing `Compensation::Wear` behaviour.\n\n**Safety floor:** changes posted `G41`/`G42` G-code and lead validation (`effort:high`).\n\n**Done means:** a quick-op finishing contour posts `G41`/`G42` wear compensation on Fanuc, Haas, and LinuxCNC posts, falls back to `Computer` on posts without cutter compensation, refuses short leads by name, and is pinned by golden post tests.\n\nPart of #3045\n",
